               <date isodate="1776" xml:id="date_aea8c84a">1776</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_c8b744ca">Copenhagen,</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_id7b2970ad">
               <p xml:id="idm39">See introduction to SchW B5:Coll.006.<lb xml:id="idm40"/>Song is on pp. 34–36; music has been signed with a 'K' and the text with an 'A'. The song is a new setting of the text appearing in Lenz 1746, no. 3. The text to song no. XIV may be sung to the present melody or that numbered XIII from Lenz 1746: 'The following successful shortening of the previous song will not be unpleasant to the connoisseurs,' and 'it is sung after one of the preceding two melodies' (p. 37). Scheibe has revised the text which has been signed with a 'Pr.'.</p>
            </history>
